# team-meta/ and logos/ are mostly runtime-synced (driver headshots/badges, team logos for every
# league, etc.) and legitimately shouldn't be committed. But a handful of small, static files
# have NO automated sync at all -- either there's no sync code for them (network broadcast
# logos), or the sync host is Cloudflare-gated and blocks the Pi's Python backend even though it
# doesn't block a one-off fetch from a dev machine (NASCAR series logos + playoff badges,
# confirmed 2026-10-01 -- see docs/ACTIVE_WORK.md). Those need to ship via git like any other
# asset, or they only ever exist on whichever machine happened to fetch them by hand.
#
# NASCAR driver photos (scripts/sync_nascar_photos.py) are the same situation, one level deeper:
# the whole nascar.com host is Cloudflare JS-challenged (not just header-checked), so only a real
# browser on a dev machine can ever fetch these -- confirmed 2026-10-02. The *_photo.png files
# and the team-meta JSON pointing at them both need to ship via git; the existing *_badge.png /
# *_headshot.png files stay gitignored and dynamically synced via the normal Setup page button
# as before (cf.nascar.com / ESPN CDN aren't Cloudflare-gated).
/team-meta/*
!/team-meta/nascar-series.json
!/team-meta/nascar-cup.json
!/team-meta/nascar-xfinity.json
!/team-meta/nascar-trucks.json
/logos/*
!/logos/networks/
!/logos/nascar/
/logos/nascar/*
!/logos/nascar/series_*
!/logos/nascar/playoffs_*
!/logos/nascar/manufacturers/
!/logos/nascar/cup/
!/logos/nascar/xfinity/
!/logos/nascar/trucks/
/logos/nascar/cup/*
!/logos/nascar/cup/*_photo.png
/logos/nascar/xfinity/*
!/logos/nascar/xfinity/*_photo.png
/logos/nascar/trucks/*
!/logos/nascar/trucks/*_photo.png
docs/

# AI / agent context files (for Grok, Claude, Cursor, Copilot, etc.)
# These are intentionally local-only and not committed.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.claude/
.github/copilot-instructions.md

